name pst-solarsystem
category Package
revision 69675
shortdesc Plot the solar system for a specific date
longdesc The package uses pstricks to produce diagrams of the visible
longdesc planets, projected on the plane of the ecliptic. It is not
longdesc possible to represent all the planets in their real
longdesc proportions, so only Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars have their
longdesc orbits in correct proportions and their relative sizes are
longdesc observed. Saturn and Jupiter are in the right direction, but
longdesc not in the correct size.
